# 🔍 Host Discovery (Ping Sweep) – Nmap Practical Analysis

## 📌 Overview

This project demonstrates **Host Discovery using Nmap Ping Sweep (-sn)** to identify active hosts within a subnet. This is a critical first step in the reconnaissance phase of penetration testing.

---

## 🧪 Command Executed

```bash
nmap -sn 192.168.18.1/24
```

---

## 🔍 Command Breakdown

| Component         | Description                                                         |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `nmap`            | Network scanning and reconnaissance tool                            |
| `-sn`             | Ping scan mode (disables port scanning, only discovers live hosts)  |
| `192.168.18.1/24` | Target subnet (256 IP addresses from 192.168.18.0 – 192.168.18.255) |

### 🧠 What This Command Does

* Sends host discovery probes (ICMP, ARP, TCP as needed)
* Identifies which systems are **alive (responsive)**
* Skips port scanning for faster execution

